# Portfolio and local SEO playbook

This rulebook balances friendly shop-owner copy with technical precision. Use it to audit and write content that can rank locally, show real work, and stay readable for both shops and developers.

## This repository (do not ignore)

This is the **matthummel** Sage 11 theme, not a generic agency case-study site. Map the playbook onto files that already ship. If it conflicts with `agency-core.mdc`, **shipping patterns win** until Matt asks to migrate.

- **Voice:** first-person **I / my**. Glossary: **shops**, **agencies**, **developers**, **learners**. Do not switch to “we/our” or “clients” (`master-content-writer.mdc`).
- **Copy location:** visitor sentences live in **Page content (theme)** (`app/page-fields.php`, `\App\field()`), posts, and comments — not hardcoded Blade except UI chrome.
- **City:** primary local market is **Gettysburg** (Adams County, Pennsylvania). Use it naturally. Do not spray city names into every heading.
- **Work:** `/projects/` is studio **example sites**, not a case-study CPT. Do not invent fake results, testimonials, revenue lifts, or client names (`docs/FEATURES.md`).
- **Proof that ships:** GitHub repos, writing, live concept URLs, profile photo. Not AggregateRating JSON-LD unless Matt asks.
- **Titles/meta:** WordPress document title and Yoast (or theme `document` helpers). Do not hardcode a second `<title>` stack in Blade. Format *when writing a title* as below.
- **Snippets:** blog posts and the Code page use existing highlight.js / `.snippet` windows. Do not add Markdown fences in Blade. Language class belongs on `<code>` in post HTML.
- **ACF:** do not treat “custom advanced custom fields theme development” as a reason to install ACF. Theme fields are `mh_f_*` in `app/page-fields.php`.
- **CTA:** one primary **Say hello** → `/contact/`. Local SEO copy must not add a second conversion funnel.
- **Layout:** do not force a 30/40/30 case-study template onto every Work card. Use that hierarchy when writing a **post** about a build, or if Matt asks for a long project page.

---

## Dual-audience targeting

Structure project write-ups and blog posts so two readers can both get value:

- **Shop / agency (non-tech):** clear outcome, plain words, what they can edit or hand over. No fake metrics.
- **Developer / peer:** stack, repo, snippets, how it ships (Sage, Tailwind, Vite, GitHub).

The home and About **audience doors** already name these people. Do not add a fifth persona.

---

## Local SEO keyword blueprint

Use these frameworks. Replace the city with **Gettysburg** unless Matt names another market. Prefer phrases that match work he actually does.

| Service pillar | Shop intent | Technical intent |
| --- | --- | --- |
| WordPress | `wordpress web design in Gettysburg` | Sage 11 custom theme, page fields, Vite — not ACF unless he asks |
| Web apps | `hire a developer for a WordPress site` | custom frontend (Sage, Tailwind, Blade), plugins, other web apps |
| Power Platform | `automate workflows with Power Platform` | custom connectors / APIs when it fits; it is **not** the main offer |

Do not stuff all three pillars into every H1. One primary phrase per page. Secondary phrases belong in body copy, once or twice.

